{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>From eternity.</b> It is the way of Scripture to join the ancients to the word עולם, as in \"מעולם אל גוי מעולם הוא\" — that is, primordial. \"I was poured out\" [נסכתי] — chosen, as in \"the princes of Sihon\" [נסיכי סיחון]." "<b>Before the earth.</b> The ancients of the earth:"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The quoted phrase combines fragments: מעולם אל appears in Habakkuk 1:12 and מעולם הוא in Micah 5:1, both illustrating עולם meaning antiquity; Ibn Ezra then turns to נסכתי (v.23) and glosses it via Numbers 21:24."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:32.335778208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}